---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import ResumeTOC from '../../components/Resume-TOC'
import TerminalPageHeader from '../../components/TerminalPageHeader.astro'
---
<Layout>
  <div class="article-inner">
    <TerminalPageHeader
      command="git log --author=joseph --reverse=false"
      title="Resume of Joseph Andrew Szczesniak"
    />

    <div class="resume">
      <ResumeTOC client:load />

      <h2 id="Summary">Summary</h2>
      <p>
        I'm an experienced software engineer, technology leader, and
        fractional CTO who loves architecting, designing, and building
        modern web and mobile applications. I've worked across fintech,
        research SaaS, entertainment, and marketing, in both high-compliance
        environments and fast-moving startups. I create and maintain code
        standards and style guides, interview and hire developers, and
        mentor teams to do their best work. I've also spent real time
        building product features on top of large language models and
        shaping ML architecture for production systems, not just chasing the
        buzzword version of AI.
      </p>

      <h2 id="Technology">Technology</h2>
      <p>
        I build full stack web and mobile applications using modern
        frameworks and tools: TypeScript, React, React Native, Astro, and
        Node.js (Express, Fastify, NestJS, and serverless on AWS Lambda),
        plus native iOS (Swift) and Android (Kotlin) when a project calls
        for it. I've also worked in Deno, Bun, .NET, Rust, and Python, and
        lean on monorepo tooling like Turborepo and PNPM alongside modern
        CSS (Grid, Flexbox, Tailwind). I contribute actively to open source
        on GitHub.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also build web services and APIs, including WebSockets and
        server-side rendering, and have real-time collaborative editing
        experience with Tiptap and ProseMirror. I work across a range of
        databases and ORMs, from PostgreSQL, MySQL, and MongoDB to Redis,
        DynamoDB, Neo4j, and Firebase, using Prisma, Drizzle, TypeORM,
        Sequelize, or Mongoose depending on the shape of the data.
        Comfortable with Test Driven Development (TDD), CI/CD pipelines,
        Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, Bicep), and cloud platforms (AWS,
        GCP, Azure, Vercel, Heroku, DigitalOcean), working across Agile,
        Scrum, and Kanban teams.
      </p>

      <h2 id="Work-Experience">Work Experience</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Mar 2026 – Present</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://br-dge.to/">BR-DGE</a>
          : Full Stack Staff Engineer
        </h3>
        <p>
          Full Stack Staff Engineer working across BR-DGE's payment
          orchestration platform: the developer-facing Web SDKs (Hosted
          Fields and Drop-In UI), the Hosted Payment Page, card vaulting and
          tokenisation, transaction routing, and integrations across
          hundreds of payment providers. Most of the merchants are gambling
          and betting operators, with fraud checks, 3-D Secure, risk
          engines, fast withdrawals, and serious transaction volume to keep
          running smoothly. Split across CI/CD pipelines, devstack tooling,
          and release engineering over a large multi-repo codebase. As the most
          senior engineer on the team, without any direct reports, I set
          technical direction, review code across the codebase, and mentor
          other engineers, and I'm usually the one pulled in on the hardest
          production issues and cross-team technical decisions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Sept 2025 – Jan 2026</p>
        <h3>AI-Powered Sales Application: Product Engineer</h3>
        <p>
          Product Engineer on an AI platform that analyzes pharmaceutical
          sales conversations with healthcare providers and turns them into
          coaching feedback for field reps, built as an offline-first
          Flutter app with encrypted recordings and a message-queue sync
          system, plus the enterprise reporting portals and admin
          applications around it. Reviewed code and coached the dev team
          building it, with some hands-on IC work of my own. Spent most of
          my time working directly with end clients and our AI/ML providers
          on the global launch plan and production scale-up, closed out the
          final integration work, and drove the architecture and technical
          design for MLflow and the rest of the ML stack.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Nov 2015 – Present</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.aureliuslab.com">
            Aurelius Lab, LLC
          </a>
          : Co-Founder &amp; Fractional CTO
        </h3>
        <p>
          Co-founded Aurelius and built an AI-powered research platform that
          helps UX and product research teams (including several Fortune
          500 companies) run end-to-end studies without the complexity of
          traditional research tooling. Designed and shipped end-user
          features powered by large language models, letting researchers
          extract, analyze, and synthesize insights across user interviews,
          survey responses, and handwritten notes. I now advise as
          fractional CTO, keeping architecture and technical direction on
          track part-time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Dec 2019 – Aug 2020</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.avantageentertainment.com/">
            Avantage® Entertainment
          </a>
          : Technical Director
        </h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          Reported directly to the CTO, in charge of multiple development
          teams and tech efforts. Helped create a scalable infrastructure,
          managed the developers, and brought standards and practices up to
          meet high security and auditing needs in preparation for UK
          Gambling Commission certification, across multiple tech stacks and
          teams.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Aug 2017 – Nov 2019</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://home.foodsby.com/">
            Foodsby
          </a>
          : Senior Software Architect and Engineering Manager
        </h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          Came in as the first FE developer and helped the team scale after
          Series A: built a CSS/React component framework, migrated the
          ordering system off a legacy .NET stack onto modernized .NET Core
          and React, and rebuilt the marketing site and internal admin
          tools. Partnered with the data science team on genetic
          algorithms for delivery route optimization. Through Series B, took
          on more management, mentorship, and higher-level architecture,
          managing the team responsible for the entire consumer-facing site
          and apps (including off-shore developers).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Sept 2016 – Aug 2017</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.ameriprise.com/">
            Ameriprise Financial
          </a>
          : Sr. Software Engineering Manager
        </h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          Managed the Interactive Marketing team's JavaScript and front-end
          engineers, responsible for all interactive marketing web assets
          and digital initiatives. Helped develop technical roadmaps
          spanning legacy systems and new third-party integrations, and led
          emerging-technology initiatives and code standards.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Apr 2015 – Feb 2016</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.primeacademy.io/">
            Prime Digital Academy
          </a>
          : Software Engineering Instructor and Agile Coach
        </h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          Taught the next generation of developers using modern
          technologies, real-world methodology, and hands-on, experiential
          learning; helped build the school's curriculum.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Sept 2012 – Apr 2015</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.nerdery.com/">
            The Nerdery
          </a>
          : Principal Software Engineer
        </h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          Designed, coded, and tested software while leading projects
          directly with clients, teams of developers, Development Managers,
          Project Managers, and QA leads. Architected everything from
          internet/extranet sites to enterprise-level solutions for Fortune
          500 companies. Founded the SharePoint development squad before
          moving into general .NET and JavaScript work, and was elected
          head of the .NET Committee, setting development standards and
          running the interview and hiring process. Shared knowledge with
          the 200+ developer team through collaboration, peer review, and
          mentorship, and created documentation, guidelines, and training
          modules.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Jan 2012 – Sept 2012</p>
        <h3>
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.atomicdata.com/">
            Atomic Data
          </a>
          : Sr. Software Engineer
        </h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          Worked with a team of developers, testers, and engineers to
          architect, design, develop, and maintain desktop applications, web
          interface systems, and custom solutions based on functional
          requirements. Maintained and monitored large SQL databases and
          SharePoint server farms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="Publications-Recognition">Publications &amp; Recognition</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">March 2018</p>
        <h3>Building Apps with Riot</h3>
        <p>
          Coauthored this practical guide to building applications with the
          lightweight Riot JavaScript framework, published by Bleeding Edge
          Press (ISBN 9781939902504).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <h3>Aurelius UX Podcast</h3>
        <p>Producer and co-host, 70+ episodes on UX research and SaaS strategy.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">Spring 2021</p>
        <h3>TinySeed</h3>
        <p>
          Member of the Spring 2021 cohort, a B2B SaaS accelerator for
          bootstrapped founders.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">2020</p>
        <h3>TechCrunch Disrupt</h3>
        <p>Selected as a TechCrunch Top Pick.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <p class="dates">July 2019</p>
        <h3>Forrester Research</h3>
        <p>
          Featured in "High-Impact Research: The Ingredients For An
          Effective UX And Design Research Practice."
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="Education">Education</h2>
      <div class="entry">
        <h3>University of Minnesota</h3>
        <p>Minneapolis, MN</p>
        <p>
          B.S., Mathematics with Specialization in Computer Applications;
          Minor in Computer Science
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="entry">
        <h3>Normandale Community College</h3>
        <p>Bloomington, MN</p>
        <p>A.A., Liberal Education with High Honors</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
  .article-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 8px;
  }
  .article-inner :global(.terminal) {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .resume {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 32px;
  }
  .entry {
    position: relative;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--surface-border);
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .entry::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -7px;
    top: 6px;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--js-color);
    border: 2px solid var(--surface);
  }
  .entry .dates {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 4px 0;
  }
  .entry h3 {
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
  }
  .entry em {
    color: var(--accent-terminal);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>
